+/// `off` makes a native-float render Store copy its readback into the guest's
+/// pages on one thread with ordinary stores, with the present conversion as a
+/// second whole-frame pass beside it, as before the Store was banded.
+///
+/// By default a Store of at least a mebibyte is split into up to four bands of
+/// whole rows, written at once with streaming stores that do not read the
+/// guest's lines first; each band converts every block of rows for the present
+/// right after copying it, while the block is still in its core's cache. The
+/// guest's bytes and the stashed frame are the same either way. Off is a
+/// refusal and never a permission.
